  <ym-title|Chapters 12\U13 dependency update><label|chapters-1213-dependency-update>

  Integrated chapters/11-restarted-history.tex immediately after Chapter11's
  clip comparison, which the fragment uses. Removed the stale placeholder
  coupling/value-recurrence discussion; retained the exact complete-source
  correction identity after the fragment.

  Chapter12 qualifications discharged:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Fixed-level background convergence: ch10:convergence, for the
    common fixed coarse endpoint.

    <item>Complete one-mark graph invariance, inverse bounds and raw
    differences: ch11:graph-estimates / graph-difference. Fine and coarse
    norms explicitly use their own \<kappa\>_i^{-1},
    \<kappa\>_i=sqrt(epsilon_i^for).

    <item>Cross-cutoff fixed-input continuity: weighted canonical paths at a
    strict width reserve and same-norm activity continuity in ch11:one-graph.

    <item>Higher-mode stopping estimate: ch11:higher-induction, exponent
    reserves and normalized root-bound, retaining original inventories.

    <item>All-order physical differences: ch11:all-period-differences. Thus
    ch12:uv-theorem now states the full cutoff limit for the selected
    trajectory with its strengthened stage requirements, rather than
    retaining those already-proved inputs as open assumptions. The
    fixed-period threshold may still depend on p. No unsubtracted
    coincident-point limit is claimed.
  </itemize-minus>

  Chapter13 qualifications discharged:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Actual finite projection kernel is Z P S_t R I, not the unscaled
    free ideal. Its rank equals the free quotient dimension exactly.

    <item>Bounded kernel families are admissible and ch11:uniform-sweep
    implies all-spectator vanishing via the common chessboard estimate.

    <item>The actual finite detector proposition supplies bounded lift
    columns at each fixed comparison depth. Include these countably many
    finite families in the same coefficient refinement before taking ordered
    limits.

    <item>Normalized null estimate for potentially unbounded trials follows
    from closure of the admissible class under bounded scalar multiplication
    and subtraction of bounded rows.

    <item>Degree inclusions are protected trials with extra factor
    a_N^(e\<minus\>d)\<less\>=1. Differences use the exact inverse-step
    cancellation and the established translated-direction reserve. Both
    obtain same-family representatives before spectators.

    <item>Centered coarse bound uses epsilon=1 in the independently derived
    sharp-centered fragment.
  </itemize-minus>

  Unchanged limitations: volume limit can require a subsequence; there is no
  uniqueness-of-volume-limit assertion, no coincident multiplication from
  field calculus, no full orthogonal covariance from this argument, and no
  extension of separated positivity to arbitrary unspecified contact terms.

  Only main11/main12/main13 edited for this integration. Chapter13 fragments
  left unchanged.

  Validation: actual-master check_draft passes with no missing/duplicate
  labels; modified environments balanced and no unexpected control bytes.
  Global LaTeX compilation remains parent's responsibility.
</body>

